# Acceptance Release Review: RELEASE-SCOPE-ID

- Acceptance fragments: task IDs, paths, versions, and hashes
- Decision refs: semantic keys and accepted versions per fragment
- Invalidation keys: bounded keys per fragment
- Approval evidence: authority and identity
- Source diff identity: commit or patch hash
- Runtime identity: environment, build, deployment, account, and role
- Evidence identity: commands, timestamps, and artifact hashes
- Reviewer identity: session or human owner

## Findings

List blocking and non-blocking findings in severity order with source or evidence references. Write `None` only after completing the checks below.

## Protected-test integrity

Record each protected path, approved hash, observed hash, and disposition.

## Requirements-test traceability

| Fragment | Requirement | Required evidence | Observed evidence | Result | Release blocking |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| TASK-ID | AC-01 | ... | ... | PASS / FAIL / MISSING | Yes / No |

## Machine verification

Record applicable static, unit, integration/contract, E2E, and non-functional commands and results. Explain every not-applicable layer.

## Engineering review

Record architecture boundaries, reuse, transactions, errors, dependency changes, unrelated changes, fallbacks, hard-coding, and observability findings.

## Human acceptance

Binding: `acceptance/human/YYYY-Www/YYYY-MM-DD-TASK-ID/binding.md` plus SHA-256

Checklist: `acceptance/human/YYYY-Www/YYYY-MM-DD-TASK-ID/checklist.md` plus SHA-256

Selected human run: `acceptance/human/YYYY-Www/YYYY-MM-DD-TASK-ID/runs/<run-id>/result.md` plus result SHA-256

Verify the run-local snapshots at `evidence/acceptance-contract.md`, `evidence/binding.md`, and `evidence/checklist.md` before accepting the signed result.

| Item | Required role | Signed observation and evidence | Result | Release blocking |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| H-01 | Product owner | ... | ACCEPTED / REJECTED / PENDING | Yes / No |

## External sandbox and runtime evidence

Record real external-system environment, identity, side effects, cleanup, and gaps. Do not substitute mock output for this section when the contract requires sandbox proof.

## Monitoring and rollback

Record metric, threshold, window, owner, response, rollback trigger, rollback command/process, and rehearsal evidence.

## Decision

- State: READY / CONDITIONAL / NOT READY / BLOCKED
- Proven scope:
- Conditions or blockers:
- Residual risk:
- Acceptance owner action:
- when hardening publication workflow -> fail closed on parser ambiguity, missing artifacts, incomplete human signoff, and unverifiable evidence; validate on a feature branch and preserve unrelated untracked `.ssot/` content [Task 2]
- when explicitly requesting merge into `main` and remote-branch deletion -> perform both and verify live remote SHA rather than stopping at a local merge [Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- A publication audit must search for actual `.tex`/`.pdf`, reconstruct every declared chunked artifact, compare declared size/SHA, and record unverifiable preflight claims separately. In the case audit, no manuscript existed; the ZIP and Base64 forms were truncated, so disposition was `scientific_closure: BLOCKED`, `evidence_integrity: INCOMPLETE`, `manuscript_state: NONE`, `technical_preflight: FAIL`, `human_signoff: PENDING`, `submission_route: UNDECIDED`. [Task 1]
- `cd src && bash reproduce_local_dynamics.sh` emitted archived values but did not cold-replay because `rebuild_local_dynamics_result.json` was missing. Generated numerical output is not proof-replay evidence when declared archive/expected records are missing. [Task 1]
- MathArc now rejects non-adjacent legacy claim pairs and duplicates; supports `\\matharcclaim{id}{revision}`; recursively collects `\\input`/`\\include` with cycle detection; blocks `.bib` without `.bbl`; and requires `INDEPENDENTLY_AUDITED` evidence plus nonempty human signoff before release-candidate readiness. Local publication tests passed 7/7, workflow policy and syntax compilation passed. [Task 2]
- `codex/publication-gates-hardening-20260831` was merged via PR #1; local and remote `main` matched `836dc6860f8f997e4e128bcd745c96b98c6b9b29`, and the remote feature branch was deleted. Untracked `agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/.ssot/` was preserved. [Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: `manuscript_state` is inferred from preflight metadata or produced numbers. Fix: inspect actual manuscript/artifact integrity first; missing paths, corrupt ZIPs, or incomplete archives are evidence-integrity blockers. [Task 1]
- Symptom: `mypy`/`ruff` are unavailable under externally managed Python (PEP 668), and a temporary venv lacks `ensurepip`. Fix: use a functioning project/bootstrap environment; do not claim checks passed. [Task 2]
- Symptom: full discovery has a failure from missing `/Users/vsiyo/Desktop/创业项目/AI4Math/registry.yaml`, or GitHub workflows never start under billing lock. Fix: report each as an unrelated environment baseline or CI-execution blocker; YAML acceptance/local tests do not establish remote CI execution. [Task 2]

